          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+functors"} category of functors
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            canonically inherits itself a monoidal category structure via a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+product"} convolution product
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Day70"} Day 70
            %em Day convolution
            products.
          %p
            In more detail, just as there is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution"} convolution
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : G \to \mathbb{C}
            whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            carries the structure of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon  \mathcal{G} \to Set
            whenever the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            carries the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
          %p
            This may be generalized by replacing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            with a more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidally+cocomplete+category"} monoidally cocomplete category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \otimes v
            preserves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in its two arguments separately; hence that the functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \otimes -
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \otimes v
            preserve colimits. This occurs notably when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal
            (so that these functors are
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ForMonoidalCategories For monoidal categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with all small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou+cosmos"} Bénabou cosmos
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C},V]
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p We discuss two equivalent ways of defining Day convolution
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#InTermsOfCoends"} In terms of coends
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#InTermsOfProfunctors"} In terms of profunctors
          %h4#InTermsOfCoends In terms of coends
          #TopologicalDayConvolutionProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, I)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %p
              Then the
              %strong Day convolution tensor product
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C},V]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\otimes_{Day}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    [\mathcal{C},V] \times [\mathcal{C},V]
                    \\longrightarrow
                    [\mathcal{C},V]
            %p
              is given by the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ×
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi V
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi V
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \otimes_{Day} Y
                    \\;\colon\;
                    c
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    \\overset{(c_1,c_2)\in \mathcal{C}\times \mathcal{C}}{\int}
                    \\mathcal{C}(c_1 \otimes c_2, c) \otimes_V X(c_1) \otimes_V Y(c_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Its unit is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi Day
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{Day}(c) = \mathcal{C}(I,-)
          %p
            We observe now that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            is equivalently a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            with respect to Day convolution.
          #ExternalTensorProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              = succeed "-monoidal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external tensor product
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{\otimes}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    [\mathcal{C}, V]
                    \\times
                    [\mathcal{C}, V]
                    \\longrightarrow
                    [\mathcal{C}\times \mathcal{C}, V]
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi V
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \overline{\otimes} Y
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\otimes_V \circ (X,Y)
                    \\,,
            %p i.e.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi V
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X \overline\otimes Y)(c_1,c_2)
                    \=
                    X(c_1)\otimes_V Y(c_2)
                    \\,.
          #DayConvolutionViaKanExtensionOfExternalTensorAlongTensor.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              product (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalDayConvolutionProduct"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              of their external tensor product (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExternalTensorProduct"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{\mathcal{C}}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \otimes_{Day} Y
                    \\simeq
                    Lan_{\otimes_{\mathcal{C}}} (X \overline{\otimes} Y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo ×
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mo ¯
                                %mi Y
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ⊗
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi Day
                                  %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\overset{X \overline{\otimes} Y}{\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    V
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\otimes}}\searrow
                    \&amp;\Downarrow&amp;
                    \\nearrow_{\mathrlap{X \otimes_{Day} Y}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathcal{C}
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            This perspective is highlighted in (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, p. 60
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalLeftKanExtensionBCoend"}
              we may compute the left Kan extension as the following
