                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CMon([\mathcal{C},V], \otimes_{Day}, y(I))
                    \\simeq
                    SymMonFunc(\mathcal{C},V)
                    \\,.
            %p In functional programming, these monoids give rise to the notion of Applicative.
            %p
              Moreover,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              over these monoid objects are equivalent to the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules+over+monoidal+functors"} modules over monoidal functors
          %p
            This is stated in some form in (
            %a{:href => "#Day70"}> Day 70, example 3.2.2
            ). It was highlighted again in (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, prop. 22.1
            ). See also MO discussion
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/130619/381"} here
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \to V
              is given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_V \longrightarrow F(I_{\mathcal{C}})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi V
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F(c_1) \otimes_V F(c_2) \longrightarrow F(c_1 \otimes_{\mathcal{C}} c_2)
            %p
              satisfying compatibility conditions. Under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of corollary
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayConvolutionViaNaturalIsosInvolvingExternalTensorAndTensor"}
              these are identified with natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    y(I) \to F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \otimes_{Day} F \longrightarrow F
            %p
              satisfying analogous conditions. This is just the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Day
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{Day}
            %p
              Similarly for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules+over+monoidal+functors"} modules over monoidal functors
          %p
          .num_remark{:id => "rmk:promonoidal functors as monoids"}
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              This page primarily addresses the Day convolution monoidal structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op},\mathcal{V}]
              when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is monoidal or promonoidal and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched"} enriched
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D}]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} biclosed
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete"} cocomplete
              there is a monoidal convolution structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D}]
              as shown in Proposition 5.4 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Day74"} Day74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C},\mathcal{D}]
              are precisely the promonoidal functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}\to\mathcal{D}
              (Remark 2.2 of
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#Day77"} Day77
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              obtains a promonoidal structure from its monoidal structure by Theorem 4.1 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Day70"} Day70
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              In the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              or pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
              and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a diagram category for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayMonoidsAreLaxMonoidalFunctorsOnTheSite"}
              are known as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
              in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayMonoidsAreLaxMonoidalFunctorsOnTheSite"}
              are known as the incarnation of ring spectra as “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors+with+smash+product"}> functors with smash product
              ”.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, section 22
            ).
          %h3#Modules Modules with respect to Day convolution
          #FreeModulesOverAMonoidInDayConvolution.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},\otimes, I)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in Mon([\mathcal{C}, V],\otimes_{Day})
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Free
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R Free_{\mathcal{C}}Mod \hookrightarrow R Mod
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              on those that are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
              and moreover free on objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (under the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Free
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Free_{\mathcal{C}}Mod
              are those of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
              are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Free
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R Free_{\mathcal{C}}Mod(c_1,c_2)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    R Mod( y(c_1) \otimes_{Day} R , y(c_2) \otimes_{Day} R)
                    \\,.
          #ModulesInDayConvolutionAreFunctorsOnFreeModulesOp.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},\otimes, I)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in Mon([\mathcal{C}, V],\otimes_{Day})
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Free
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %msup
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mod_R \simeq [R Free_{\mathcal{C}}Mod^{op}, V]
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of right modules
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of that of free
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeModulesOverAMonoidInDayConvolution"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, theorem 2.2
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_idea Proof idea
            %p
              Use the identification from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayMonoidsAreLaxMonoidalFunctorsOnTheSite"}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
              and of any
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+object"} module object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              as a functor with the structure of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monoidal+functor"} module over a monoidal functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N(c_1) \otimes R(c_2) \longrightarrow N(c_1 \otimes c_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that these transformations have just the same structure as those of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functoriality
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
